Reference material (no source code copied):
- rockbenben/subtitle-translator, MIT: https://github.com/rockbenben/subtitle-translator — architecture and format behavior; its language list includes ckb. Its README notes context-aware translation is LLM-only.
- subsrt-ts, MIT: https://github.com/rakuzen25/subsrt-ts — parser package considered; this project uses independently written parsers to retain original timings and format details.
- google-translate-api-x, MIT: https://github.com/AidanWelch/google-translate-api — previously used; no longer included.
- Subtitle Edit: https://github.com/SubtitleEdit/subtitleedit — UX reference only, no code copied.
Dependencies and their licenses are available in package-lock.json and the respective packages.

- morluto/rea, MIT: https://github.com/morluto/rea — methodology reviewed; no REA code copied or bundled.
- JSZip, MIT or GPL-3.0 (MIT selected): https://github.com/Stuk/jszip — dependency for client-side ZIP export.
- subtitlestranslator.com and translatesubtitles.co — public descriptions used for UX research only; no code copied.

- Google website translation widget protocol: independently implemented based on public discussion https://github.com/ssut/py-googletrans/issues/268 and rockbenben/subtitle-translator; the embedded widget key is public, not a user credential.

- Anthropic frontend-design and webapp-testing skills: https://github.com/anthropics/skills — design and testing guidance reviewed; no skill source code copied.
- Puter.js, Apache-2.0: https://github.com/HeyPuter/puter — online speech-to-text SDK; Gemini receives audio via Puter. The postal-mime dependency is overridden to a patched release.
- Long-form transcription design guidance: https://dev.to/hanna_altunina/how-to-build-a-reliable-long-form-transcription-pipeline-59l0 — boundary overlap and checkpointing considered; no code copied.
- bidi-js, MIT: https://github.com/lojjic/bidi-js — test-only Unicode bidirectional algorithm to verify punctuation positioning in LTR and RTL contexts.
- W3C bidirectional text guidance: https://www.w3.org/International/geo/html-tech/tech-bidi.html — direction-mark research; no code copied.

- Vazirmatn font by Rastikerdar, SIL Open Font License 1.1: https://github.com/rastikerdar/vazirmatn — bundled using @fontsource/vazirmatn for offline display.

- Claude translation skill research (no source copied or runtime skill bundled): https://github.com/roshaw/claude-translation-agency (MIT) — terminology consistency and quality gates; https://github.com/shuji-bonji/s1000d-translate-skill (MIT) — segment boundaries and validating protected placeholders. These are LLM-oriented workflows, not translation engines.

- Kurdish alphabet reference (no code copied): https://badini.app/badini-alphabet — Hawar and Arabic-script letter correspondences; the mapping in this application is independently implemented and approximate.
